<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:50:09Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Macron says limiting Ukraine aid would pave way to 'another war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47093946c4b9018b8b9391e7f71f68bf27d399b600a9215cbec9ab4ec8eacdc0</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:49:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:15:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-macron-says-limiting-ukraine-aid-would-pave-way-to-another-war--f4035bbf29fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-macron-says-limiting-ukraine-aid-would-pave-way-to-another-war" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Saturday warned that limiting aid to Ukraine would force Kyiv into an "unjust peace" and risk another war. His statement comes as the United States pushes ahead with efforts to negotiate between Ukraine and Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Elon Musk's SpaceX aborts booster recovery due to technical issues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11b3a0af63ce81d3a565aec41d5918b8586e165a633a37b66a3b579288988287</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:49:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:33:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/elon-musk-s-spacex-aborts-booster-recovery-due-to-technical-issues--6420a1fd1469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/elon-musk-s-spacex-aborts-booster-recovery-due-to-technical-issues" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk's SpaceX is in the midst of a 15th test-flight of its Starship rocket. The company was hoping to pull off the first-ever "double catch" - with both the booster and the ship itself coming safely back down to earth. Instead, an unspecified problem forced the company to abort recovery of the booster, which was diverted from its return path and crashed down into the Gulf of Mexico. Analysis by journalist Frédéric Castel, based in Bosa Chica, Texas, USA.</summary></entry><entry><title>Youth Olympic Games organisers hail Senegal's capability to host major events</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72731aa44671af3c950f942894119077dce0bbf43fc046a3cab77cf633ba1001</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:49:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:25:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-organisers-hail-senegal-s-capability-to-host-major-events--044ed43c0324.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-organisers-hail-senegal-s-capability-to-host-major-events" /><summary type="html">Dakar 2026 is over. Two weeks of competition, thousands of young athletes and a historic first for Africa. The Youth Olympic Games brought the world to Senegal for the first Olympic sporting event ever held on the continent. From record-breaking performances to historic medals for the host nation, Dakar 2026 has been a celebration of sport, youth and cultural exchange. Our correspondent Aminatou Diallo reports from Dakar.</summary></entry><entry><title>France and Cambodia share their love for pétanque in Phnom Penh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b6def855f7eaf6a0b1feca0ee5568efd0541b31f3b87229ed5839ffd74eaa42</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:49:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:23:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-france-and-cambodia-share-their-love-for-p_tanque-in-phnom-penh--035fb864e2c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261114-france-and-cambodia-share-their-love-for-p%C3%A9tanque-in-phnom-penh" /><summary type="html">Phnom Penh is hosting the 20th Francophonie Summit this Sunday and Monday. French President Emmanuel Macron is attending as part of a 3-day state visit to Cambodia. France and Cambodia's history is deep rooted and complex, but the two countries have one thing in common: a love for pétanque. Story by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Washington divided over how to deal with fallout from the Nvidia case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7285ab730cc05c03eac488bef770053f9bfb4213825bc5b68200cb461face6d9</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:49:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/washington-divided-over-how-to-deal-with-fallout-from-the-nvidia-case--10e578662d3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/washington-divided-over-how-to-deal-with-fallout-from-the-nvidia-case" /><summary type="html">After the fall, the fallout. US government agencies are squabbling after AI leader Jensen Huang stepped down from chips giant Nvidia in disgrace. The Treasury says it wanted to blacklist a Singapore company at the heart of the scandal, but the Commerce Department didn't act. Megaspeed was run by suspected Chinese spy Alice Huang, who reportedly had an affair with Jensen Huang. Details by Peter O'Brien.</summary></entry><entry><title>US: What exactly caused the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b3456026197342f4f6edc9c97ce9a6b7bc6a95dc5988249598915acca9ac77e</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:49:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T16:35:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-what-exactly-caused-the-longest-nationwide-ground-stop-in-25-years--773fa7defb8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-what-exactly-caused-the-longest-nationwide-ground-stop-in-25-years" /><summary type="html">After a nearly five-hour ground stoppage, flights in the US have resumed. However, officials are warning that it will take days to recover from the ongoing delays related to the incident. Transport Secretary Sean Duffy explained the crisis was due to a failure in ageing telecommunications equipment. What exactly happened? Answers with FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Transport Secretary asks Congress for $30 bn to upgrade aviation infrastructure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84ab39fec25aa5a1558663c081fb9ed71229272dbf5d03160b419d8a04cb254d</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T16:32:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-transport-secretary-asks-congress-for-30-bn-to-upgrade-aviation-infrastructure--1fa408877d9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-transport-secretary-asks-congress-for-30-bn-to-upgrade-aviation-infrastructure" /><summary type="html">A failure in aging telecommunications equipment Friday forced a nationwide halt to departures from US airports. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin says officials have found no evidence so far of a cyberattack, but that they're not ruling it out. Details by Jack Pownall.</summary></entry><entry><title>Wales claim historic victory against All Blacks for first time since 1953</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1379a5c6cc286108db6d897031bdc4b1efa409eaa82f7d2ca2d9be35d478f82</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:50:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T16:27:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261114-wales-claim-historic-victory-against-all-blacks-for-first-time-since-1953--94ffeb4f1023.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261114-wales-claim-historic-victory-against-all-blacks-for-first-time-since-1953" /><summary type="html">Wales claimed a historic 35-28 victory over New Zealand in Cardiff on Saturday, securing their first win over the All Blacks since 1953.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>'Poisoned chalice': French presidential hopeful Riner rebuffs Macron's backing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfec918653770a943ed9a0479f7263ba982ecd7134487c1383716f8a4dba8791</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:50:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T14:57:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-judo-star-and-presidential-hopeful-riner-calls-macron--dd2a958e7c7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-judo-star-and-presidential-hopeful-riner-calls-macron" /><summary type="html">French judo champion Teddy Riner on Saturday publicly distanced himself from President Emmanuel Macron, calling his endorsement a "poisoned chalice". The presidential hopeful seeks to position himself as an alternative to France's political extremes.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo, Rwanda clash over Francophonie leadership as Macron seeks compromise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d7c33a8f960d6ff0279e80cc3294542f16a36516106eecdc6864448f15ca193</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T14:54:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261114-dr-congo-rwanda-clash-over-francophonie-leadership-as-macron-seeks-compromise--8dd812a22403.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261114-dr-congo-rwanda-clash-over-francophonie-leadership-as-macron-seeks-compromise" /><summary type="html">DR Congo and Rwanda clashed Saturday over the leadership of the Francophonie, as tensions between the neighbouring countries spilled into the race to head the 53-member organisation. French President Emmanuel Macron urged Rwanda to withdraw its candidate in favour of a compromise choice ahead of Monday's vote.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'I never imagined my father was a Nazi': Born in a German-run 'baby factory'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3e3b8259c96791266cb572077f1db26280ab3cfdb6d46c1490c02f930a2275e</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T13:25:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-i-never-imagined-my-father-was-a-nazi-born-in-a-german-run-baby-factory--a90ba69f5562.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261114-i-never-imagined-my-father-was-a-nazi-born-in-a-german-run-baby-factory" /><summary type="html">Two trainloads of children, some of them born in Nazi-run "Lebensborn" maternity homes, were brought from Germany to Commercy in eastern France in 1946. One of those on board was Édith Pagot.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>USA: All passengers survive after tanker hits docked river cruise ship in New Orleans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:708ee2a38c5f93cd0b3c5737ffd908f9cd5bdf1ae4cfc7d1837b8cc4a3d41fba</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T13:15:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans--196361a3fb34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans" /><summary type="html">A portion of the Mississippi River remains closed after a collision between an oil tanker and a riverboat forced a chaotic river rescue in Louisiana. Story by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Inside Ethiopia's war: Rare access to a hospital treating victims of renewed fighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4664c5f311d35bfca09329e74ee05d58a0ac341ab4d740d0a95754ddf0d3b374</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:23:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/inside-ethiopia-s-war-rare-access-to-a-hospital-treating-victims-of-renewed-fighting--64d2eb5d22c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/inside-ethiopia-s-war-rare-access-to-a-hospital-treating-victims-of-renewed-fighting" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's renewed conflict is taking an increasing toll on civilians, with humanitarian organisations reporting a rise in casualties. In the Amhara region, FRANCE 24’s correspondent Tom Canetti was granted rare access to a civilian hospital where surgeons are struggling to treat the influx of wounded patients. But for many caught in the fighting, reaching medical care is a challenge in itself.
 
Warning: The report contains images of surgery that may be confronting for some viewers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb036ad315c7ec5415d8eeed3b3a9d0a524f459dbef12e6b4ce1d44f7c6b0cf3</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world--0c414d784e65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world" /><summary type="html">From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry><entry><title>U2 releases first new studio album in a decade, 'Caranaval de Luz'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b251da2362731685930e2c67c5134daa4d34cec48ade47a998a13fd425f0220</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:17:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/u2-releases-first-new-studio-album-in-a-decade-caranaval-de-luz--7856f7336f02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/u2-releases-first-new-studio-album-in-a-decade-caranaval-de-luz" /><summary type="html">U2 just released a new album after nine years of no new content. And fans are already rocking out to the new songs. Details on the Irish rock band’s comeback by Ophelie Jacobson.</summary></entry><entry><title>Half a million people gather for an open-air mass by Pope Leo in Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae9809d805e9674460b677cfc7cd61c73983ee96fbb61268aafef2b429a98f96</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru--865ee0c1d4cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo said it was a "joy to be back" in his second home of Chiclayo, where he made his name as a bishop. This is the latest stop on his South America tour, the very tour that saw fears of cancellation after the Pope underwent surgery for lung cancer. Story by Vedika Bahl.</summary></entry><entry><title>Microsoft's widespread outages caused global chaos, including in the healthcasre industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49cbf80b1da9a5356eb930acf1137235261d2aa41f0bc815d3688e4ab54c4e01</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:07:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/microsoft-s-widespread-outages-caused-global-chaos-including-in-the-healthcasre-industry--b5a2d510401d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/microsoft-s-widespread-outages-caused-global-chaos-including-in-the-healthcasre-industry" /><summary type="html">Microsoft says it is seeing improvements in its service availability after an hours-long disruption knocked out its platforms including Outlook and Teams. The outage has affected hundreds of millions of people across the globe. The healthcare industry was among those impacted, as Ophelie Jacobson explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>France fend off South African comeback to clinch long-awaited win in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d563168f459761cabdb70f4ae088b33814beaa19b04f43f89ca0b512ac5e2473</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:58:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261114-france-fend-off-south-african-comeback-to-clinch-long-awaited-win-in-paris--eb24a1ccaa69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261114-france-fend-off-south-african-comeback-to-clinch-long-awaited-win-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Twenty-one years after last beating the Springboks in Paris, Les Bleus held out for a 21-19 win over the world champions on Friday after a nailbiting finale. Antoine Dupont and company are now one step away from reaching the Nations Championship final in London.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>US proposed Ukraine cedes Donbas in exchange for joining NATO, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:459968ee36563ebc9b73ff9fa241601cfa71e63dc37b3d345270e80b07b767d2</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership--b3597e97289d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">President Zelensky said the US had proposed ceding Ukraine's eastern city of Donbas to Russia, in exchange for Ukrainian membership of NATO, following the latest round of peace talks in Abu Dhabi this week. He reiterated that Kyiv was not willing to retreat from its territory and warned that the Kremlin's bid to change the continent's security architecture could lead to more wars.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Climate action is alive': Triumphant Democrats attend COP31 summit shunned by Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bbcbb9c9c5a55d8f6155be9d8f4be32cb15b1a4d93db18fc32860f693cdb916</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:25:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261114-climate-action-is-alive-triumphant-democrats-take-on-cop31-shunned-by-trump--38a7ef55fd3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261114-climate-action-is-alive-triumphant-democrats-take-on-cop31-shunned-by-trump" /><summary type="html">A delegation of 18 Democratic lawmakers arrived at the COP31 climate summit in Turkey on Saturday to reaffirm the US commitment to tackling global warming following their sweeping midterm election victory.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX's Starship encounters problems during 15th test flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:503bca1e39099657ef96dc04e2f839fab01bda055e72cea3702e603d712f1700</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:21:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spacex-s-starship-encounters-problems-during-15th-test-flight--0ef99121135e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spacex-s-starship-encounters-problems-during-15th-test-flight" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk’s SpaceX successfully launched its Starship, the world's largest spaceship, into orbit where it should release 15 satellites for its Starlink network. A few minutes after lift off however, the rocket's booster which was meant to return to the pad splashed down in the Gulf of Mexico. Details by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Can Nvidia survive without tech titan Jensen Huang?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dde671524b506ecc596f309a39f9a79d6f67f15c5776ce286f52665cf283facb</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:20:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/can-nvidia-survive-without-tech-titan-jensen-huang--9cf2241e07bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/can-nvidia-survive-without-tech-titan-jensen-huang" /><summary type="html">The Financial Times says computing giant Nvidia has approached Rene Haas, CEO of British chip designer Arm, in its search for a potential successor to Jensen Huang. Huang resigned after his affair with an alleged Chinese spy. Meanwhile some employees are clamouring for Huang's return – as his fellow tech leader Elon Musk. A sign of Huang's lingering star power, in an industry where so often the fate of each giant company depends on one man. Story by Peter O'Brien.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's school principals say threats and violence have become unbearable</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4398cf4ae6617a993e5b3dd49dfb34b4a72abc032a3e135ca1b278323f093c9</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:17:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-school-principals-say-threats-and-violence-have-become-unbearable--2f046ff96317.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-school-principals-say-threats-and-violence-have-become-unbearable" /><summary type="html">Headteachers gathered across France this Friday, to demonstrate their frustration after nearly two months of student protests that have blockaded high schools. Many of the teachers support the students, but say they feel exhausted and isolated as the violence has surged. They are calling the government to protect them. Story by Vedika Bahl.</summary></entry><entry><title>France protests for fifth Saturday against living costs and heavy-handed policing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a8a0c3e0ac0c47619801bacb6ab50fcdd4ce714fcd9c8f5acade76e2167cea5</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:48:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:15:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-protests-for-fifth-saturday-against-living-costs-and-heavy-handed-policing--dabdfccbee08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-protests-for-fifth-saturday-against-living-costs-and-heavy-handed-policing" /><summary type="html">Different causes are set to come together for one march in Paris this Saturday. Campaign groups, students and Yellow Vest protesters are due to join forces in the capital, bringing together demands on wages, education and civil liberties. But after weeks of demonstrations, union leaders warn that protest fatigue is setting in, while police officers are seeking better compensation for the risk of policing the protests. Story by Jack Pownall.</summary></entry></feed>
